  "slug": "3-ingredient-lemon-blueberry-angel-bars-recipe-11971542",
  "name": "3-Ingredient Lemon Blueberry Angel Bars",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "These 3-ingredient lemon blueberry angel bars are bright lemon bars loaded with blueberries They lie somewhere between a classic lemon bar and angel food cake, with a nice crumb, and a little bounce.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C). Coat a 13x9-inch baking pan with baking spray. Stir together lemon pie filling and cake mix in a large bowl until combined; gently fold in blueberries. Transfer mixture to prepared pan and spread into an even layer."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until a wooden pick inserted in center comes out clean, 25 to 30 minutes. Let cool completely in pan on a wire rack, about 2 hours. Dust with powdered sugar, if using, and garnish with lemon zest, if using. Cut evenly into 12 bars. Recipe developed by Craig Ruff"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 25,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 5,
